            "controller_support": "full",
            "detailed_description": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Werewolves shooting fireballs at each other!</h2><br><i>Lupinball</i> is a hilariously hectic 2-to-4-player deathmatch, which starts out like dodgeball but slowly becomes a bullet hell. Power up and blast your foes in their fuzzy faces, but here's the key: fireballs zoom around the arena forever, bouncing off walls and speeding up over time. The arena gets insanely chaotic in seconds, as everyone shoots more and more and <strong><i>more</i></strong> fireballs! Last wolf standing wins.<br><br>Which fluffy fighter will be the survivor among the fiery doom?<br><br><strong><i>Join the official Lupinball Discord server! </i></strong><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >A fast, frantic, four-player flurry of fur... locally or online!</h2><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Power up, then smash your enemies in the face with magic fireballs! As wolves!<br></li><li>Local and online multiplayer, with full Steamworks integration! Build up wins and earn a place on the Leaderboard!<br></li><li>Awesome, catchy soundtrack from the one and only <i>Fox Amoore</i>!<br></li><li>Use a shield that reflects enemy shots and stuns enemy wolves, adding further depth and strategy!<br></li><li>Every stage is an absurd theme that affects the gameplay, such as a dark haunted house, a farm with gale-force winds, or a warehouse with pits of fire!<br></li><li>Break open item crates! You can block everyone else from powering up, teleport around the map, or even flip the screen upside down!<br></li><li>A single-player score attack mode, with Leaderboard! How many points can you attain?<br></li><li>Streamers: our Twitch extension (in the Muxy Overlay) provides a live scoreboard and lets viewers vote for their favorite player in real-time!</li></ul>",
            "about_the_game": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Werewolves shooting fireballs at each other!</h2><br><i>Lupinball</i> is a hilariously hectic 2-to-4-player deathmatch, which starts out like dodgeball but slowly becomes a bullet hell. Power up and blast your foes in their fuzzy faces, but here's the key: fireballs zoom around the arena forever, bouncing off walls and speeding up over time. The arena gets insanely chaotic in seconds, as everyone shoots more and more and <strong><i>more</i></strong> fireballs! Last wolf standing wins.<br><br>Which fluffy fighter will be the survivor among the fiery doom?<br><br><strong><i>Join the official Lupinball Discord server! </i></strong><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >A fast, frantic, four-player flurry of fur... locally or online!</h2><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Power up, then smash your enemies in the face with magic fireballs! As wolves!<br></li><li>Local and online multiplayer, with full Steamworks integration! Build up wins and earn a place on the Leaderboard!<br></li><li>Awesome, catchy soundtrack from the one and only <i>Fox Amoore</i>!<br></li><li>Use a shield that reflects enemy shots and stuns enemy wolves, adding further depth and strategy!<br></li><li>Every stage is an absurd theme that affects the gameplay, such as a dark haunted house, a farm with gale-force winds, or a warehouse with pits of fire!<br></li><li>Break open item crates! You can block everyone else from powering up, teleport around the map, or even flip the screen upside down!<br></li><li>A single-player score attack mode, with Leaderboard! How many points can you attain?<br></li><li>Streamers: our Twitch extension (in the Muxy Overlay) provides a live scoreboard and lets viewers vote for their favorite player in real-time!</li></ul>",
            "short_description": "Werewolves shooting fireballs at each other! Survive each round as it becomes more and more chaotic from everyone's fireballs bouncing around non-stop. Be the last wolf standing in this hilarious 2-4 player arcade deathmatch, local or online!",
            "supported_languages": "Inglês, Português (Brasil), Russo, Chinês simplificado",
            "reviews": {
                "query_summary": {
                    "num_reviews": 1,
                    "review_score": 8,
                    "review_score_desc": "Very Positive",
                    "total_positive": 50,
                    "total_negative": 3,
                    "total_reviews": 53
                },
                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "50523798",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198019466684",
                            "num_reviews": 784,
                            "playtime_forever": 55,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 18,
                            "last_played": 1690918626
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[table][th]\nReview by Sven Evil - Steam's largest local 4-player curator! See 100s of more local 4-player reviews at my [url=http://store.steampowered.com/curator/8485829-SvenEvils-Playground/] curator page[/url]! \n[/th][/table]\n\nOften simple games prove to be the best games. \n\nA good example is Lupinball. It's setup is wonderfully simplistic, it is easily understandable so anyone is able to play within seconds. 4-player doge-ball anyone?\n\nFirst you have to collect 3 randomly spawning orbs to charge up a fireball. Then you shoot the fireball at your friends. Any hit is deadly, even from your own fireball.\n\nThe speciality is this: If you miss, the fireball does not disappear, but bounces around the screen (until someone is hit by it). You can now collect three orbs again and shoot another fireball. Very soon the screen is full of fireballs bouncing around!\n\nSimple? Yes!\nFun? LOTS OF!!!\n\nDifferent stages, some spawning boxes with different extras and the ability to use your orbs to power up a shield add some variety. The game also has a certain charm with its retro-style graphic, quirky characters and funny loading-screen tips!\n\nLupinball plays great with only two players, something that cannot be said about all single-screen 4-player games. But for the full mayhem, play it with 4 players!\n\nLupinball can be enjoyed by both local and online players. Best way to find online players is Lupinball's discord server. Single player is possible... but not recommended.\n\nGame worked fine with 4 Xbox One controllers.\n\n[u][b] Conclusion:[/b][/u]\nPerfect ‘pick up and play‘ party game for 4 players!",
